  "description": "Wing B is inside the project. On Tuesday at 10:00 wing B is normalized under literal comparison and the project under the fixture fire-rating interpretation, so the interpretation in force for Door 101, in wing B, is ambiguous, and for Door 102, in the project only, it is the fire-rating interpretation. Finish stories for both doors (paint against stain) continue when A-601 changes both finishes to brown-paint on Wednesday: under every candidate the sides still disagree. Door 101's generated detection records interpretation null with a normalization key listing both normalizations; Door 102's records the fire-rating interpretation and no normalization key. An application's review may carry the key beside a null interpretation, whatever the interpretation in force for its subject, but not beside a named interpretation or in another shape.",
  "note": "5.5.5: \"Where the comparison named none and the interpretation in force was ambiguous (7.3.8), `interpretation` and `interpretation_version` are `null`, and the frame also carries `normalization`: `{ \\\"ambiguous\\\": [ ... ] }`, listing exact references to the normalizations concerned, ordered as in 7.6.6, so that it is never read as literal comparison. Write validation checks a recorded frame's shape only, never whether it agrees with the interpretation in force (7.2.4).\" 2.4.4, `@frame` row: \"its key `normalization` only beside a `null` interpretation, for an interpretation in force that was ambiguous\". README section 7: \"Where that interpretation is ambiguous, `interpretation` and `interpretation_version` are `null` and the frame also carries `\\\"normalization\\\": {\\\"ambiguous\\\": [refs]}`, listing full references to the normalizations concerned, ordered as in 7.6.6 (5.5.5). The key is absent otherwise.\" The reviews cite the Assertions in effect at their effective times, Wednesday's from A-601 and Monday's from the specification, so that they leave each story's current comparison evidence unchanged. 7.3.5: \"The *current comparison evidence* of a reviewed story has changed when its sides disagree at the cutoff and their applicable values differ from the values its review cited. Then 7.3.1 applies, and a new related story is opened, beginning no earlier than the review's effective time.\" A review citing Monday's A-601 Assertion after Wednesday's change would open such a related story, which this fixture does not test.",
